{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>In your flesh.</b> \"Flesh\" is the designation for the generative organ in the sacred language, as in גִּדְלֵי בָשָׂר (Ezekiel 16:26), זָב מִבְּשָׂרוֹ or הֶחְתִּים בְּשָׂרוֹ מִזּוֹבוֹ (Leviticus 15:2–3), and others. This is because the sign of the covenant being on this organ — which brings about perpetuity of the species — indicates the perpetuity intended in the covenant; and its being the generative organ means that the sign upon it indicates the continuation of the covenant upon the children."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:30:29.296398882Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}